  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#name-binding",
  "description": "Name binding claim verification (avalon_protocol::shard_identity::verify_name_binding_claim). A claim binds a name to a self-certifying id, signed by the key the id certifies. The signed message is the ASCII tag avalon-name-binding-v1 (no length prefix), the id as u32-BE length plus UTF-8, the 32 raw key bytes, the name as u32-BE length plus UTF-8 and created_at as i64 BE unix seconds. A claim verifies only when the key hashes to the id (node: plus the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the key) and the signature is strict Ed25519 over those bytes (S >= L and a small-order R or key are rejected). signingKeySeedHex is a fixed non-secret seed. Generated by scripts/gen-sth-witness-vectors.py.",
